Manage file metadata using the recon-toolkit container (exiftool,
mat2, pdfid, oletools).

Two execution modes:
  server (--server URL or $USULNET_API_URL set) — POST to /api/v1/metadata/jobs.
  local  (default when no server is configured)  — run the toolkit container
                                                  directly against the host
                                                  Docker daemon.

Usage:
  usulnet meta [flags]
  usulnet meta [command]

Available Commands:
  extract     Print the metadata for one file as JSON / YAML / table
  scan        Extract metadata for every file under <dir> (recurse with --recursive)
  strip       Write a cleaned copy of the file (default: <path>.stripped)

Flags:
  -h, --help             help for meta
      --image string     toolkit image (local mode only; default $USULNET_RECON_TOOLKIT_IMAGE)
      --server string    usulnet API URL (forces server mode; default $USULNET_API_URL)
      --timeout string   container timeout (e.g. 30s)
      --token string     API token (default $USULNET_API_TOKEN)

Global Flags:
  -c, --config string   config file path (default: /etc/usulnet/config.yaml or ./config.yaml)
      --json            shortcut for --output json (overrides --output)
      --output string   output format: table|json|yaml (default "table")
  -q, --quiet           suppress informational output (errors and primary data still print)

Use "usulnet meta [command] --help" for more information about a command.
